{title: Til Pondering Turns To Praise}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 78}

Verse 1
[A]This is an honest retrospective of my daily walk. I wrote this just a couple of
days before my 51st birthday (and sang it as a special the next evening, as I was
scheduled to sing a solo Sunday night, with instrumental backup of our praise band).
I hope it blesses and encourages anyone else who acknowledges that we don't have
all the answers, but we know and trust the One who does.

Verse 2
The recording was done on 4 tracks. The chorused, 12-string guitar effect was done
by recording 2 guitar tracks with the same 6-string, except the 2nd time it was played
a key lower and capo'd 2. Other than applying some compression on each track, no other
effects (reverb, etc) were added to the mix.

Verse 3
Til Pondering Turns To Praise
Words and Music by Larry Holder
Copyright (C) 2010 Larry Holder

Verse 4
The [D]longer that [F#m]I live
[G]The less I really [D]know
Of [Em]how all things [G]have come to be
And which [D]way they [A]will go
Yet still [G]I know [E]You're faithful
[A]And on [D]this journey, [A7]too,
[G]To give [Em]us daily manna
[A]And lead my steps to [D]You...

Refrain
Sometimes [G]it is my [D]unbelief
Sometimes [A]it is the [Bm]veil
[F#]That [G]keeps us from [Bm]the perfect [D]sight
That one [Em]Day will prevail
[G]Until that day, Lord, [A]hold my hand
[D]And lead me thru the [G]maze
Til [Em]questions lead to [A]answers
And pondering [A]turns to [D]praise.

Verse 5
Without your grace and [F#m]mercy
[G]I'd surely quickly [D]fall
[Em]You are my faithful Savior
[Bm7]You are [D]my All in [A]All
If I [G]will only [A]listen
And seek [D]Your face in [G]prayer
You [Em]promise You will [A]answer
[F#m]And peace is [A]waiting [D]there...

Refrain
[D]Sometimes [G]it is my [D]unbelief
[A]Sometimes it is [B]the veil
[C#]That keeps [G]us from [Bm7]the perfect [D]sight
That [Em]one Day [E]will prevail
[G]Until that day, [A]Lord, hold my hand
[D]And lead me thru the [G]maze
[D]Til [Em]questions lead to [A]answers
And pondering [A]turns to [D]praise.
